      "message": "On a fresh MBP, my SDK location is `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk`.\n\nAccording to Gemini:\n\n\"The difference between the two paths is that \"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/Developer/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk\" is the older, more detailed path to the macOS SDK within the Command Line Tools, while \"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk\" is the newer, simplified path that most modern Xcode installations will use, essentially removing the \"Platforms\" directory layer; it\u0027s generally recommended to use the latter path in most cases today.\"\n\nSee also https://github.com/hedronvision/bazel-compile-commands-extractor/issues/68",
